      "cve": "CVE-2026-110757",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-110757"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "Text::CSV_XS versions before 1.65 for Perl allow record splitting by writing strings used as numbers without quotes in combine.\n\ncombine and print do not check whether a field needs quotes when its value has Perl's integer or numeric flag set. Perl sets these flags on a string used in a numeric operation when it parses as a number, which allows leading and trailing whitespace. With binary set, as csv does by default, \"12\\n\" passes a check such as $qty \u003e 0 and is then written unquoted with its newline.\n\nA value validated as a number can end the record early and turn the fields after it into a separate row.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
