    {
      "cve": "CVE-2026-110759",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-110759"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "Text::CSV_XS versions before 1.65 for Perl return a 0xFF byte that is not in the input for an empty last field followed by a lone CR in parse.\n\nWhen the input to parse ends in a separator and a lone CR, the parser treats the end of the input as the next character and stores the end-of-file marker in the field as the byte 0xFF. With binary set, parse(\"a,\\r\") returns the fields \"a\" and \"\\xFF\". On UTF-8 flagged input the last field is a UTF-8 flagged string holding that lone byte, which is malformed UTF-8. The same input with a non-empty last field is rejected as an error.\n\nA CRLF file read line by line and chomped ends this way when its last column is empty, so the application receives a byte that is not in its input.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
